  "runtime_policy_detail": "Automatic production calibration, never filtered by its measured value. GOGC=100 for scenes; unchanged ordered harness sets GOGC=300. GOMEMLIMIT=off, GOMAXPROCS unset (runtime default); worker overrides unset. Startup calibration, snapshot work and warmup excluded from timer but recorded. Caches persist from scene phase into ordered warmup; ordered harness clears seed cache at start. Fresh process per variant/block.",
  "declared_utc": "2026-11-18T03:38:15.887927+00:00",
  "hypothesis": "Corrected PR boundaries retain correctness before FK optimization lands; quantify the cost of stricter validation and the subsequent FK/collision gains. The earlier six-block full-stack and PR4 comparison remain separate and unchanged.",
  "primary_baseline": "Hash-frozen original native executable, using its ordinary native selection; never forced CBiRRT.",
  "intermediate": "Unmodified current main 8ab5892be050dadb5de3b140b6ee9ea212984f51; each preceding cumulative PR head is also an incremental comparator.",
  "candidate": "Corrected cumulative PR1, PR2 and PR3 heads; required dense angular sampling, exact geometry identity and unsafe clearance-skip removal now precede FK optimization.",
  "stopping_rule": "Complete all three matched independent blocks, 15 serial fresh processes, regardless of results or desktop activity. Each process has 25 measured seeds per scene, one complete ordered warmup and three measured ordered passes. Stop only for execution failure or user interruption; retain unfinished attempts. No optional stopping or selective reruns.",
  "policy": "Ordinary automatic production calibration; default workers, geometry, constraints, sample grids and required validation. Fresh process caches; scene phase precedes ordered phase. Same inline audit schedule; frozen original-geometry offline audit after all timing.",
  "practical_targets": {
    "stack_vs_original": "At least 3% lower total replay time for unique scenes and 15% for the ordered workload, with all returned stack plans accepted. Report estimates and uncertainty even if targets are missed.",
    "increments": "3% total-time reduction is a useful per-PR latency change. PR 1 is primarily correctness/lifetime work and may cost time. Compare each head to its predecessor as well as original native; do not add or infer phase-time gains.",
    "tail_quality": "Report all acceptance failures, median/p95/p99/max, >=1/5/30s counts and per-input path-length distributions. More than 10% worsening of p95/p99 or within-input path-length p95 is a review flag. Do not silently weaken validation.",
    "deployment": "Retain the earlier >=10% total-time benefit in both workloads, no correctness failures and no >10% tail/path-quality regression gate. This exploratory shared-desktop comparison is not a deployment certification."
  },
  "inference": "Exploratory exhaustive paired process-block bootstrap (3^3=27 resamples), with three independent initializations per variant. Fixed equal weights for 11 unique scenes; duplicate08 remains in the ledger with zero headline weight. Preserve within-process ordered dependence. Seeded randomized cyclic order gives different positions per variant but is not fully counterbalanced. Multiple comparisons/endpoints are exploratory; no formal statistical-significance, precise-tail or equivalence claim. Do not pool with earlier six-block data.",
  "admission": "Observe host load, active tools, power and thermal state before and approximately every five seconds during every process. Record-only: no admission wait and no stop because of desktop load, builds, power changes or advisory thresholds. User explicitly requested a comparison under available conditions. The operator launches no unrelated builds/tests/profiles/heavy analysis during timing. Keep every attempted request and every process; report all observed interference.",
